.TH CALCULATOR 1 "2025-01-15" "MPC v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
calculator \- add two integers and output the sum
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calculator
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I number1
.I number2
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B calculator
utility takes two integer arguments and outputs their sum to stdout.
It performs basic integer addition and includes error handling for invalid inputs.
The program reads exactly two integer arguments from the command line,
adds them together, and prints the result followed by a newline.
.PP
If either argument cannot be parsed as a valid integer, the program
will exit with an error message and non-zero status code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information showing usage and available options, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output except the result. Error messages are still shown.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add two positive integers:
.nf
.RS
$ calculator 42 13
55
.RE
.fi
.PP
Add negative and positive integers:
.nf
.RS
$ calculator -10 25
15
.RE
.fi
.PP
Display help information:
.nf
.RS
$ calculator --help
Usage: calculator [OPTIONS] <number1> <number2>
Add two integers and output the sum.

Options:
  -h, --help     Display this help message
  -v, --version  Display version information
  -q, --quiet    Suppress verbose output

Examples:
  calculator 42 13    # outputs: 55
  calculator -5 10    # outputs: 5
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B calculator
exits with one of the following values:
.TP
.B 0
Success. The two integers were added successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments. One or both arguments could not be parsed as integers.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong number of arguments provided.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B calculator
may produce the following error messages:
.TP
.B "Error: Invalid integer: 'xyz'"
The specified argument could not be parsed as a valid integer.
.TP
.B "Error: Expected exactly 2 arguments, got N"
Wrong number of command-line arguments provided.
.TP
.B "Error: Integer overflow"
The result of the addition would exceed the maximum representable integer.
.SH NOTES
The calculator uses signed 64-bit integers, supporting values from
-9,223,372,036,854,775,808 to 9,223,372,036,854,775,807.
.PP
Hexadecimal (0x prefix) and octal (0 prefix) number formats are not supported.
Only decimal integers are accepted.
